{
 "id": "mms_boussinesq_2d",
 "capability": "F4a",
 "title": "Planar Boussinesq MMS (gravity -e_y): coupled u, p, T with O(1) buoyancy, variable mu and k, rho0 c_p != 1, T_ref != 0, Dirichlet / Robin / Neumann temperature BCs, both viscous forms, Galerkin and SUPG; structured and distorted nested meshes; Newton",
 "physics": "rho0 (u.grad)u - div sigma_form = f_u + rho0 beta g (T - T_ref) e_up, div u = 0, rho0 c_p u.grad T - div(k grad T) = Q",
 "levels": [
  "mms"
 ],
 "run": {
  "runner": {
   "module": "f4a_heat",
   "function": "bous_mms_planar",
   "check_module": "f4a_heat_check",
   "cost": "long",
   "timeout_s": 10800
  },
  "parameters": {
   "field": {
    "path": "tools/fluids_mms/out/bous_sq.json",
    "sha256": "1698f275bd257006e89586fa686f1c7c6c1762071db2b85d4bdee4e522493c7c"
   },
   "element": {
    "velocity": "P2",
    "pressure": "P1",
    "temperature": "P2"
   },
   "viscous_forms": [
    "lap",
    "sym"
   ],
   "convective_form": "standard (F2a's required form)",
   "energy_advection": "convective form a u_h.grad T (a = rho0 c_p)",
   "constants": {
    "rho0": "5/4",
    "cp": "6/5",
    "beta_g": "2",
    "T_ref": "1/3"
   },
   "gravity": "-e_y",
   "temperature_bcs": {
    "x0": "dirichlet",
    "y1": "dirichlet",
    "x1": "robin",
    "y0": "neumann"
   },
   "velocity_bcs": "Dirichlet (exact data) on every wall",
   "dirichlet_data": "P2 (P1) Lagrange NODAL interpolation of the fixed callables at the vertices and edge midpoints of the Dirichlet boundary parts; at a node shared by two Dirichlet parts the data agree (one exact callable per field); Dirichlet beats every natural condition at a shared node",
   "supg_energy": "Residual-based SUPG: add sum_K int_K tau_K (a b.grad v) R_K(T_h) (r-weighted in axisymmetry) to the Galerkin form, with the FULL element residual R_K(T) = a b.grad T - div(kappa grad T) - s evaluated element-wise (second derivatives of T_h for P2, the grad kappa. grad T term, and in axisymmetry the hoop term kappa T_r / r). FIXED FAMILY: tau_K = C tau_rule(h_K) with tau_coth(h) = h / (2 p a |b|) (coth Pe - 1/Pe), Pe = a |b| h / (2 p kappa), or tau_Shakib(h) = [(2 p a |b| / h)^2 + 9 (4 p^2 kappa / h^2)^2]^(-1/2) (C multiplies tau; it is NOT inside Pe or h); p the element degree; |b| the Euclidean norm of the advecting velocity (in axisymmetry its MERIDIONAL part (b_r, b_z)); tau evaluated at the quadrature points or as an element constant; h_K a length that depends on the element's GEOMETRY only (invariant under a renumbering of its vertices and under rigid motions); admissible pairs (C, h_K): c_adv = C h_K / sqrt(2|K|) in [1/2, 2] AND c_diff = C h_K^2 / (2|K|) in [1/2, 2] (the advective- and diffusive-limit tau relative to C = 1, h_K = sqrt(2|K|)), evaluated on the right isosceles triangles of the unit, channel, pipe and annulus families; the same (rule, C, h_K) is used on every fixed mesh; on the distorted family the per-element values may leave the box (longest edge x 1: c_diff in [1.37, 3.07]), immaterial for its Pe 1e6 items (advective limit: only c_adv matters). Examples: h_K = sqrt(2|K|) (NGSolve mesh_size; MFEM sqrt(T->Weight()) on an affine triangle) with C in [1/2, 2]; the longest edge (sqrt(2) sqrt(2|K|) on the fixed right triangles) with C in [1/(2 sqrt 2), 1] (C = 1 is the library's shakib_hK); MFEM GetElementSize(e, 0) = 1.0746 sqrt(2|K|) with C in [0.47, 1.73]. In the coupled problem b = u_h.",
   "quadrature_requirement": "Every Galerkin and SUPG integrand that is a polynomial on affine triangles is integrated EXACTLY: for P2 T and v: a b.grad T v with b in P1 degree 4 planar / 5 axisymmetric; with b = u_h in P2 (the coupled energy equation: B, C1, E1, H1, X1) or the quadratic Poiseuille b (G1, G2) degree 5 planar / 6 axisymmetric (a degree-4 rule for a u_h.grad T v moves X1 by 3.4e-8 against its 1e-8 recipe); the momentum terms as F2a requires. Non-polynomial data (MMS loads, Robin T_ext, Neumann data) by rules of degree >= 6 on elements and edges; the identities that involve such data are then QUADRATURE-LIMITED (worst measured 1.3e-11 with an admissible degree-6 rule, against bounds of 1e-10). Data callables are evaluated at interior quadrature points and at the Dirichlet nodes only (some axisymmetric loads have removable 1/r singularities on the axis). Coupled: the F2a requirement for the momentum equation.",
   "meshes": {
    "unit": {
     "family": "unit",
     "N": [
      8,
      16,
      32,
      64,
      128
     ],
     "h_nominal": [
      0.125,
      0.0625,
      0.03125,
      0.015625,
      0.0078125
     ],
     "construction": "scalar_transport_check.box_mesh(8, 8, k), k = 0..4, on [0,1]^2 in (x, y): 8 x 8 squares split along the (1,1) diagonal except the two cells at the corners (1,0) and (0,1) (split the other way: no triangle with all vertices on the boundary), refined uniformly (red) k times (identical to the fixed F1a structured_mesh(N), N = 8 * 2^k). Nested.",
     "h_definition": "h_nominal = 1/N (leg of the right triangles); h_max = sqrt(2)/N reported too"
    },
    "distorted": {
     "family": "distorted",
     "refinements": [
      1,
      2,
      3,
      4,
      5
     ],
     "h_nominal": [
      0.125,
      0.0625,
      0.03125,
      0.015625,
      0.0078125
     ],
     "construction": "scalar_transport_check.distorted_mesh(k), k = 1..5, on [0,1]^2 in (x, y): 4 x 4 base mesh, interior vertices displaced by (0.2/4) U(-1,1)^2 (numpy PCG64(20261101)), refined (red) k times. Nested; element Jacobians vary.",
     "h_definition": "h_nominal = 0.25 / 2^k"
    }
   },
   "nonlinear_solver": {
    "start": "the Dirichlet lift: the P2 Lagrange nodal interpolant of the data at the Dirichlet nodes and 0 at every other node, p = 0",
    "method": "Newton with the exact Jacobian of the coupled residual (every coupling block: d(buoyancy)/dT, d(u.grad T)/du, d(convection)/du), full steps, no line search",
    "newton_rtol": 1e-12,
    "newton_maxit": 30,
    "linear_solver": "direct sparse LU",
    "history": "solver.history = [{kind, residual, step}] after every step"
   },
   "pressure": "no constraint given: the solver detects the constant-pressure nullspace",
   "variants": "lap/sym x Galerkin/SUPG (tau of the pinned family) on the unit family; lap/sym Galerkin on the distorted family (planar)"
  }
 },
